WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:20.104
"Nora?" Henry called. "Wait! What are you talking about?"

2
00:00:20.105 --> 00:00:22.663
"Who cares?" Maggie said.

3
00:00:22.664 --> 00:00:27.828
"We care," Henry said. "What if Nora took that painting?"

4
00:00:27.829 --> 00:00:31.644
Cole gasped. "That actually makes sense!

5
00:00:31.645 --> 00:00:35.484
Well, as much sense as anything Nora ever does, anyway.

6
00:00:35.485 --> 00:00:41.698
Nora seemed really upset when she heard Nathan's painting might end up in the museum."

7
00:00:41.699 --> 00:00:44.286
"Exactly," Henry agreed.

8
00:00:44.287 --> 00:00:48.576
"And the stuff she was saying a minute ago made her sound guilty."

9
00:00:48.577 --> 00:00:52.701
"So are we adding her to the suspect list?" asked Maggie.

10
00:00:52.702 --> 00:00:54.851
"Definitely," Cole said.

11
00:00:54.852 --> 00:00:59.102
"She's sneaky enough to snatch that painting and hide it somewhere."

12
00:00:59.103 --> 00:01:05.446
"Luckily, we already know she's not very good at covering her tracks," Henry said, smiling.

13
00:01:05.447 --> 00:01:11.341
He was talking about an earlier case involving Nora, which had led to her adopting Patches.

14
00:01:11.342 --> 00:01:14.552
"Let's go look for clues at the scene of the crime."

15
00:01:14.553 --> 00:01:18.584
"Okay." Maggie put out the Closed sign again.

16
00:01:18.585 --> 00:01:21.903
"How much time do we have before judging starts?"

17
00:01:21.904 --> 00:01:28.401
Henry glanced at his phone. "Almost an hour."

18
00:01:28.402 --> 00:01:30.830
They hurried over to the art show.

19
00:01:30.831 --> 00:01:36.432
When they arrived at the empty spot where Nathan's painting had been, Nathan wasn't there.

20
00:01:36.433 --> 00:01:38.821
But someone else was.

21
00:01:38.822 --> 00:01:43.423
"Hi, Mr. Collins," Henry said. "What are you doing?"

22
00:01:43.424 --> 00:01:48.800
Mr. Collins spun around and laughed sheepishly. "Oh! You startled me."

23
00:01:48.801 --> 00:01:52.413
"Were you looking for Nathan's painting?" Maggie asked.

24
00:01:52.414 --> 00:01:57.160
"Yes, I admit it." Mr. Collins tugged on his flowered tie.

25
00:01:57.161 --> 00:02:00.861
"It's been on my mind ever since I saw it this morning.

26
00:02:00.862 --> 00:02:05.360
Can you believe two artists found such similar inspiration?

27
00:02:05.361 --> 00:02:08.933
Young Nathan's subject could be the twin of mine!"

28
00:02:08.934 --> 00:02:15.666
"Um, okay." Cole sounded doubtful. Henry knew what his friend was thinking.

29
00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:19.991
Mr. Collins' crazy cat painting looked nothing like Nathan's!

30
00:02:19.992 --> 00:02:24.243
"What if the judges think your paintings are too similar?" Maggie asked.

31
00:02:24.244 --> 00:02:27.616
"Are you worried they might not pick yours for the museum?"

32
00:02:27.617 --> 00:02:32.054
"I suppose not." Mr. Collins winked and smiled.

33
00:02:32.055 --> 00:02:37.273
"Nathan and I are not even in the same age category, in case you couldn't tell.

34
00:02:37.274 --> 00:02:40.065
I'm just worrying over nothing, as usual!

35
00:02:40.066 --> 00:02:43.358
It's the curse of being a sensitive artist."

36
00:02:43.359 --> 00:02:48.582
He glanced at the empty spot. "So where is your friend's masterpiece?"

37
00:02:48.583 --> 00:02:54.463
"We're not sure," Henry said. "It disappeared about forty minutes ago."

38
00:02:54.464 --> 00:03:00.470
"Oh dear!" Mr. Collins looked alarmed. "Is there an art thief at the show?"

39
00:03:00.471 --> 00:03:05.019
"Maybe," Cole said. "Have you seen anything suspicious?"

40
00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:07.841
"Where have you been for the past hour?"

41
00:03:07.842 --> 00:03:11.517
Maggie demanded before Mr. Collins could respond.

42
00:03:11.518 --> 00:03:16.924
Henry winced. Sometimes Maggie could sound rude when she questioned people!

43
00:03:16.925 --> 00:03:23.632
Mr. Collins looked surprised. "Am I a suspect? Luckily I have an alibi."

44
00:03:23.633 --> 00:03:27.748
"You do?" Henry was glad the man didn't seem insulted.

45
00:03:27.749 --> 00:03:35.039
Mr. Collins nodded. "I've been at Mrs. Sweet's booth for the past hour or so, learning how to make candy.

46
00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:37.470
She could tell you that too."

47
00:03:37.471 --> 00:03:43.066
"Okay," Henry said. "Well, we'd better get back to investigating."

48
00:03:43.067 --> 00:03:46.244
The Lemonade Detectives hurried away.

49
00:03:46.245 --> 00:03:49.693
"Are we going to check his alibi?" Maggie asked.

50
00:03:49.694 --> 00:03:54.088
Henry shrugged. "I suppose we should, just to be sure.

51
00:03:54.089 --> 00:03:56.902
But I bet he's telling the truth."

52
00:03:56.903 --> 00:04:02.642
"Yeah," Cole agreed. "His alibi explains why we couldn't find him earlier."

53
00:04:02.643 --> 00:04:04.957
They walked toward the crafts fair.

54
00:04:04.958 --> 00:04:08.348
As they passed the bandstand, Henry spotted Owen.

55
00:04:08.349 --> 00:04:12.661
"Hi," Henry greeted him. "Have you seen Patrick?"

56
00:04:12.662 --> 00:04:17.874
Owen frowned. "Not since I saw you guys earlier," he said.

57
00:04:17.875 --> 00:04:21.540
"We were supposed to meet at the crafts fair ten minutes ago.

58
00:04:21.541 --> 00:04:27.015
When he didn't show up, I came here to see if he was at the burger stand. But he wasn't."

59
00:04:27.016 --> 00:04:31.557
Just then Henry noticed a tall, thin figure moving through the crowd.

60
00:04:31.558 --> 00:04:36.231
"Look," he said. "It's that strange woman!"

61
00:04:36.232 --> 00:04:38.379
"Quick! We have to catch her!"

62
00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:42.000
Cole took off, with Henry and Maggie right behind him.

63
00:04:42.001 --> 00:04:45.857
The woman was walking quickly toward the museum at the edge of the park.

64
00:04:45.858 --> 00:04:50.017
"Excuse me!" Henry yelled. "Wait up!"

65
00:04:50.018 --> 00:04:52.124
The woman glanced back.

66
00:04:52.125 --> 00:04:57.300
When she saw Henry and the others coming, she gasped and dashed toward the museum.

67
00:04:57.301 --> 00:05:00.610
She ran up the steps, disappearing inside.

68
00:05:00.611 --> 00:05:03.009
"Stop!" Maggie yelled.

69
00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:09.009
The Lemonade Detectives ran into the museum. It was cool and dim inside.

70
00:05:09.010 --> 00:05:15.362
The sound of footsteps echoed off the walls, but Henry couldn't tell which direction they were coming from.

71
00:05:15.363 --> 00:05:18.499
"This way!" Cole cried, pointing.

72
00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:23.063
Henry turned just in time to see the woman disappear around a corner.

73
00:05:23.064 --> 00:05:27.658
He ran after her and burst into a large room filled with sculptures.

74
00:05:27.659 --> 00:05:30.851
"Where'd she go?" Maggie exclaimed.

75
00:05:30.852 --> 00:05:34.021
"There!" Henry cried.

76
00:05:34.022 --> 00:05:39.223
The Lemonade Detectives followed the woman through the next room, which was filled with paintings.

77
00:05:39.224 --> 00:05:43.564
Then she escaped into a hallway with lots of doors.

78
00:05:43.565 --> 00:05:50.937
Cole glanced at all the doors. "Which way did she go?" he asked breathlessly.

79
00:05:50.938 --> 00:05:54.289
A door leading outside was swinging shut.

80
00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:59.689
Henry hurried over and looked out into the Belltown Arts Day crowd.

81
00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:05.033
He sighed. "I think we lost her."
